{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 22, :comments ["<b>And the magicians of Egypt did so with their secret arts.</b> After the waters were smitten through Moses and Aaron, from where did the magicians find water to turn into blood? The answer is that not all the waters were turned to blood by the decree of Moses and Aaron — only the waters that were in the river (יאור), as it says: ״הנה אנכי מכה במטה אשר בידי על המים אשר ביאור ונהפכו לדם״, and it is written: ״וירם במטה ויך את המים אשר ביאור לעיני פרעה ולעיני עבדיו ויהפכו כל המים אשר ביאור לדם״ — it does not say 'all the waters of Egypt' but 'all the waters that were in the river.' And likewise it is written: ״ולא יכלו מצרים לשתות מים מן היאור״, and if so, they still had water from the rivers and from the pools. And this cannot be said, for explicitly the verse says: ״על מימי מצרים על נהרותם על יאוריהם ועל אגמיהם״, and it is written ״ויעשו כן משה ואהרן״. And what it says — ״ויך את המים אשר ביאור״ and it does not say 'all the waters of Egypt' — is the word of HaShem, may He be exalted, because the river was the head of them all, and all the other rivers and pools draw from it, and when he smote the river and its waters turned to blood, all the other waters that draw from it turned to blood as well. If so, from where did the magicians find water to turn into blood? The answer is that they would dig in the ground and bring up water and turn it into blood, for the decree of Moses and Aaron applied only to places where the waters collect in the open, and the decree did not apply to waters beneath the ground. Or perhaps what it says — ״ויעשו כן״ — is all a counterfeit act, for once the magicians heard the warning that Moses and Aaron had forewarned Pharaoh in this manner beforehand, they hastened to places where the water had not yet turned to blood, and they made it appear as though they were doing so with their secret arts, and they would say that this was done by their power — when certainly it was not turned by their word, but only by the decree of Moses and Aaron. This is what is written: ״ויעשו כן חרטומי מצרים בלטיהם״ — meaning a counterfeit act. And therefore you will find that in the case of Moses and Aaron it mentions ״לעיני פרעה ולעיני עבדיו״, but it does not say so in the case of the magicians." "<b>Or</b> it is possible to interpret according to the verses of the parashah that the Holy One, blessed be He, commanded two things: one, the striking of the river with the staff so that its waters would turn to blood, and second, the stretching out of the hand with the staff without striking, upon the other waters of Egypt — upon the rivers, upon the streams, and upon the pools — and they would become blood. And what it says, ״הנה אנכי מכה במטה אשר בידי״, the intent is upon Aaron, for Moses does not strike the river, neither in the plague of blood nor in the plague of frogs. And it says ״ויעשו כן משה ואהרן כאשר צוה ה׳ לבאר״, for both of them fulfilled His command: Moses forewarned Pharaoh concerning the plague of the river, and told Aaron to stretch out his hand over the waters of Egypt, and Aaron did so — he stretched out his hand over the waters of Egypt just as HaShem, may He be exalted, told Moses. And this is what is written: ״וירם במטה״ — Aaron raised his hand with the staff and stretched his hand toward the four winds of the world over the waters of Egypt, for so the Holy One, blessed be He, commanded Moses: ״נטה את ידך והך במטה את המים אשר ביאור ויהפכו כל המים אשר ביאור לדם״. And therefore it returns and mentions at the end: ״ויהי הדם בכל ארץ מצרים״ — meaning, through the power of the stretching out of the hand; and this comes to teach that the waters of the river turned to blood by the power of the striking with the staff, and the blood in the other waters was through the power of the stretching out of the hand."], :book :exodus, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 7, :notes {0 "The comment interiorly cites multiple Exodus verses without explicit references; all left as in the original Hebrew quotations without added citations."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:57:02.081498022Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}